I had a feeling my first post on RGRN would be a YAFAP.
I've had Nethack for almost a year now, playing on and off til about  
January when I became rather addicted. I've now read most of the spoilers  
on Eva Myer's site (not recommended, I reckon it'd be a lot more fun to  
play unspoiled. Ah well), lurked on RGRN for the last month or so, and  
lost many a promising character to horrible, stupid deaths. Just like  
everyone else, I'd guess :P

Last week I started Orange, the same day I started and lost about five  
other valkyries. The unfortunate thing about my story is that there's  
nothing really interesting about it. She got lucky with a magic whistle,  
BoH and amulet of reflection in the Mines (didn't know about the ammy till  
i finished sokoban and #called that one). Found the bones file of my last  
promising valk, who'd fallen through a trap door wielding a c corpse (i  
even knew it was there, too!) chipped at her statue with my trusty  
pick-axe to retrieve Mojo and strength gloves. An unattended altar a few  
lvls later helped uncurse everything and I set up a junk/polypile stash.  
Just after sokoban a red naga dropped me a WoW and I knew that, barring  
unfortunate accidents with cockatrices, this was a definite ascension  
candidate. +2 SDSM, +2 cloak of MR, trekked between Medusa and my stash on  
Dlvl 15 looking for polypile fodder. A session with my wand (do you always  
get a /oPoly in Sokoban? my last few chars have) gave me 2(!) extra BoH's,  
a magic marker (yay!) some speed boots, and i got to see my pets change  
into geckos, spiders, elf-lords and finally an Incubus and Ice Devil.  
>Slightly< better than a bloody gecko. And no, I didn't #chat with my tame  
Incubus. That's just wrong.

Can't remember if I did the Quest or Medusa first. Probly the quest.  
Bloody easy too, 3 throws of my Mojo and Lord Surtur went down. Didn't  
even get to move off his starting square. Medusa's titan was peaceful.  
Wished for a ring of levitation, bludgeoned Medusa to death, cleared one  
lvl of maze and opened the castle with one of my 2(!) magic flutes (both  
 from adjacent levels in the gnomish mimes). Castle gave me a hawaiian  
shirt, a black dragon (yummy), silver and grey dragon scales (didn't need  
to wish for that SDSM after all) and little else. My incubus died in the  
Valley. Ice Devil killed the first priest of moloch, no worries. Dropped  
all my junk and buffed myself up for Gehennom: had to wish for scrolls of  
enchant armor as I hadn't seen >any< all game. Danced with 3 scrolls worth  
of nurses in the corridor between the altar and the downstairs, genocided  
mind flayers, master mind flayers, and all L, drunk a few pots o' healing,  
replaced my +3 orcish helm with a +2 helm o' telepathy (1 b?oEA took it to  
+5, too. Didn't know that was possible). ~250 hp and -45AC, i headed into  
hell. Paid off Asmodeus and Baelzebub ("cowardly mortals" eh? How about  
stupid demons?), killed Juiblex in about 4 hits and made it to Orcus's  
town. My furthest character before this was a Samurai who rampaged through  
the town with a c corpse, before dying in the temple doorway. The 'e' key  
is too close to 'w'. I've learnt from that SD. Orcus went down in a few  
hits and I continued along, now with 2 or 3 /oDeath. Killed Vlad, no  
worries. The wizard's tower thingo was pretty easy, found another scroll  
to genocide V for good measure. Rodney took a few hits from Mojo before  
being zapped with a death ray. No patience for you. Did the invocation  
thing, cleared out the sanctum no worries. That cockatrice came in handy,  
and i didn't do anything stupid with it. Rotted away before I could get  
the High Priest, so I had to kill him traditionally. Started the Ascent,  
named amulet in hand. 4 scrolls of gold detection? check. Plane of earth,  
no worries. Air? Ring of conflict comes in handy. Fire, also no worries.  
Water was weird, I had no idea how the bubble thing worked. Lost the  
location of the portal and stumbled through it with my ring of conflict  
still on. Whoops. The Titan on Astral summoned one round of nasties before  
being zapped. The death ray hits the Titan! You kill the Titan! You kill  
the cockatrice! Cockatrice hey? yeah, why not. Death in the centre,  
Pestilence to the right. Pestilence got stoned along with a lot of angels  
and priests. Chaotic. Death's door was open so I took him on next. Lawful.  
Stood on the altar, copied my save game for prosperity (:P) and offered  
the amulet. Phew.

What have I learnt? New chars are gonna resist looking up the spoilers,  
the game oughta be more fun that way. A pick-axe is your friend. Valk's  
are goddamn easy, especially if you get lucky. And now that I've finally  
done it, I can stop playing this stupid game so much and pay attention to  
my fiancee. I'll just start a new archaeologist.....



